Z||000000||Pretender||03-15-2000||11:31 PM||||A whopping 147MPH!, why is this the fastest fiero? i'm sure that if i had a 5spd. in my car and a different set of gears i'd come darn close to that record. If i can hit 120+ in my auto w/ 2 cracked manifolds why is the 147mph the magic number to beat? I'm not dogging this guys or his car but it makes me wonder how that car can have the record. Things that make you go hmmmm...<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||03-16-2000||01:23 AM||||That is pretty lousy...  Find a 5-sp V6 with the highest possible gear ratio.  Lower it a bit.... free flowing intake and exhaust.... Maybe lose a few pounds and you're there. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||03-16-2000||09:15 AM||||I can pace my Alfa 164 w/ it's speed o reading 141... and with NO drag on the dyno 150 @ 6000rpm bouncing off the rev limiter... Who are these people to know he right people and get in the record books?? Wish I knew who to talk to.. There was another post saying the quickest stock normaly aspirated GT was like 15.6 in the 1/4. Wish i knew what their interpretation of stock was/is. I can do that and miss a shift!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> haven't heard that song in a while... "Things that make you go humm.."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||03-16-2000||11:12 AM||||As I was reading about some of the high top speed runs of Corvettes and the like I started to think about the problems they were having and how they relate to Fiero. The most interesting topic was the situation happening in the Vette when the air going through the radiator is forced down under the car. At high speeds this build a high pressure area just below the hood where air can't get out of the way fast enough. The front end feels like its lifting up. Those of you with V8s have probably felt this at some point or another at varying degrees of severity. 147 mph being THE fastest a Fiero can go? Not likely. <BR>I seem to remember that number being the speed  someone hit with a 4 cyl (Not a SD block) on the salt flats. V8 Fieros hit that speed with a tach loafing around probably around 3000. The fastest Ive heard before they got out of it was somewhere north of 170 with a 91 Vette engine and still had lots of Go left in it. John Norman probably holds the title with his NOS Northstar.<P>You start going that fast and aerodynamics will make you or break you. Facinating stuff!||||reg||1
Z||000004||87ECO5||03-16-2000||12:56 PM||||Now, is this with or without all those stickers everyone is talking about!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||03-16-2000||06:30 PM||||Oh! I almost forgot! They did studies at the University of Brevity Studies they proved that the size of the stickers on your car corresponds with the amount of horsepower that you gain. Example: Sticker going across your hood: 10 HP. As opposed to the sticker that simply goes on your door: 5 hp. Further studies have also concluded that having your 2 inch exhaust end with a 6 inch exhast tip gives you a 2 second advantage in the 1/4 mile and a 5 mph increase. These findings can be found in almost any Import Performance magazine. <BR>    Some Fieros have reportedly been seen trying to conduct their own experiments on a more subtle level with exhaust and wheels. Some of these experiments have been known to go horribly wrong. The end result is a Fiero with gold spoke Daytons with an exhaust that can only be described as comical. <BR>   <BR>Don't let this happen to you. Protect your Fiero from these heinous experiments. ||||reg||6
Z||000006||Greg Piet||03-16-2000||06:44 PM||||So am I now a ricer???  Since I got an official number from the SCCA (its 47 by the way), I went and put numbers on my Fiero since it looks better than the masking tape I was using.  So now I have a 20 hp increase since I have 2 numbers on each door?   COOL!<BR>I still dont have the coffee can exhaust, but I can do that if im now officially a ricer.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||03-16-2000||06:51 PM||||No, No, No, Greg.<P>To get these HP gains the sticker can NOT be for a useful purpose. It either has to be for an aftermarket product (perferably one that is NOT installed on your car) or for a different factory designation (perferably one that was not available for your year or model).||||reg||12
